  ],
  "description": "Splitting a sliced order into slices (place_sliced_order, before anything is sent). input.quantity, max_slice_quantity, lot_size, freeze_quantity (GetSecurityInfo frzqty) and the slices are all in trade units on every exchange, MCX included. The largest slice is floor(frzqty / lot) * lot units (a slice may equal frzqty); max_slice_quantity (null: none) lowers it and must be a whole number of lots; a freeze_quantity of null, 0 or negative is unknown, and max_slice_quantity is then required (a frzqty that is not an integer fails the GetSecurityInfo read before planning). expected is the list of slices (as many full slices as fit, then the remainder), or {\"error\": \"ValueError\"} when an argument is invalid (quantity, lot_size, max_slices or max_slice_quantity not an integer >= 1, booleans refused; quantity not a whole number of lots), the largest slice is below one lot, the freeze quantity is unknown without max_slice_quantity, or more than max_slices slices are needed.",
  "source": "tradesmart._slicing.plan_slices",
  "tolerance": {}
}
